'''Cantham House''' was the private estate of [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] on [[Coruscant]]. A penthouse suite independent from the rest of [[Imperial Executive Building|its building]], it contained a few bedrooms, a great room, and a crescent-shaped balcony that looked out on a wide swath of the cityscape. By either [[senator]]ial or [[Monarchy|royal]] standards, it was considered relatively modest.<ref name="Leia" /> The roof of Cantham House was protected from high winds by large [[glass]] slabs that had scenes of [[Alderaanian]] [[mountain]]s etched into them.<ref name="QH">''[[Queen's Hope]]''</ref>

During a soirée Organa hosted in<ref name="QH" /> [[22 BBY]]<ref name="Date">''Queen's Hope'' is set ten [[Standard year|years]] after the [[Battle of Naboo]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[32 BBY]]. Therefore, ''Queen's Hope'' and the soirée must be set in [[22 BBY]].</ref> on the roof of Cantham House the disguised handmaiden [[Sabé]] saw Alderaanian [[plant]]s and pieces of art that incorporated wind or [[water]] she noted that it must have cost a fortune but Alderaan had been a member of the [[Galactic Republic]] for a very long time.<ref name="QH" />

Toward the end of the [[Clone Wars]], Organa and his fellow [[senator]]s [[Mon Mothma]] and [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] organized [[Cantham House meetings|meetings]] at Cantham House<ref name="Visual Guide" /> to discuss the [[Petition of 2,000]], a set of demands by the [[Delegation of 2,000]] group of representatives who were concerned with the state of [[democracy]] in the [[Galactic Republic]]<ref name="Rebel Files">''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref> that included [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]]'s relinquishment of his wartime emergency powers as the [[Supreme Chancellor]]. However, Palpatine refused to let go of his powers at the end of the war and further declared himself [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] succeeding the Republic.<ref name="Visual Guide" />

In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="MoFDate">{{MOFdate|60}}</ref> following the [[attack on the Executive Center]] and Organa's sponsorship of the [[Imperial Rebirth Act]], the Alderaanian senator and the [[Alderaanian monarchy|Queen of Alderaan]] [[Breha Organa]] retreated to Cantham House. A group of protesters gathered outside, battering at doors and windows, demanding his arrest for treason against the [[Galactic Empire]] and issuing [[death]] threats against the couple.<ref name="MoF">''[[Reign of the Empire: The Mask of Fear]]''</ref>

House security lowered [[blast plate]]s, which secured the entrance. The protesters continued through daybreak, and the senators repeated calls to the police were ignored. At this point, a [[gunship]] approached Cantham House, manned by three [[clone trooper]]s pointing their weapons downward, and led by a [[Tarsunt]] [[Unidentified Tarsunt admiral|admiral]] who was a friend of Bail Organa. The admiral ordered the troopers to fire at the crowd, and most of the mob managed to flee the scene.<ref name="MoF" />

In [[3 BBY]],<ref name="LPOA Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa's]] birth in [[19 BBY]]. The events of ''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]'' commence just after Organa's sixteenth [[birthday]], which places the events of the novel in [[3 BBY]].</ref> when Organa's adopted daughter Leia Organa joined the [[Apprentice Legislature]] she stayed in Cantham House rather than a dorm like the rest of her fellow [[Apprentice Legislator]]s.<ref name="Leia" />

During the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the Galactic Empire, after Mothma condemned Palpatine for his actions during the [[Ghorman Massacre]], the [[Imperial Security Bureau]] arrived at Cantham House to interview [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] and several other individuals due to suspicions the Bureau had about them.<ref name="Rebel Files" />

